  ## FAQs
  
  ### What is the best AI tool for creating TikTok videos?
  
  For most creators, **CapCut** is the best free option — it's made by TikTok's parent company and stays current with trends. For AI-generated videos from text, **InVideo AI** and **HeyGen** are the leaders. For an all-in-one workflow that includes scheduling, try [PostEverywhere](https://posteverywhere.ai/).
  
  ### Can AI tools help me go viral on TikTok?
  
  AI tools improve your odds by helping you post consistently (the #1 algorithm factor), write better hooks, add captions for accessibility, and identify [optimal posting times](https://posteverywhere.ai/blog/best-time-to-schedule-tiktok-posts). But virality also depends on content quality, trend relevance, and audience connection. Read our full guide on [how to go viral on TikTok](https://posteverywhere.ai/blog/how-to-go-viral-on-tiktok) for the complete strategy.
  
  ### Are free AI tools good enough for TikTok?
  
  Yes. A combination of CapCut (free), ChatGPT (free), and PostEverywhere's free tier gives you editing, scripting, and scheduling at $0. Many successful TikTok creators started with free tools before upgrading as they grew.
  
  ### What is the best AI tool for TikTok captions?
  
  **Captions App** is the standalone leader for animated, trendy captions. **CapCut** includes solid auto-captioning for free. **Submagic** adds B-roll suggestions alongside captions. For most creators, CapCut's built-in captions are sufficient until you need specialized styles.
  
  ### How do I schedule TikTok posts with AI?
  
  Use a scheduling tool like [PostEverywhere](https://posteverywhere.ai/social-media-scheduler) that supports direct TikTok publishing. Upload your video, use the AI caption generator for your text, select your optimal posting time, and schedule. The tool posts automatically. See our step-by-step guide on [how to schedule TikToks](https://posteverywhere.ai/blog/how-to-schedule-tiktoks).
  
  ### Can AI tools replace human creativity on TikTok?
  
  No, and they shouldn't. AI handles the repetitive tasks — captioning, scheduling, basic editing, script drafts — so you can focus on the creative decisions that make content uniquely yours. The most successful TikTok creators use AI as an assistant, not a replacement.
  
  ### What AI tools do professional TikTok creators use?
  
  Most professional creators use a stack of 3–4 tools: an editor (CapCut), a caption tool (Captions App or Submagic), a scheduler ( [PostEverywhere](https://posteverywhere.ai/social-media-scheduler) or Later), and a writing tool (ChatGPT). High-volume creators add repurposing tools like OpusClip. See our guide on [staying consistent on social media](https://posteverywhere.ai/blog/how-to-stay-consistent-on-social-media) for workflow tips.
  
  ### How much should I spend on AI tools for TikTok?
  
  Start at $0 with free tools and scale up as you see results. Most solo creators spend $20–$60/month total. Businesses typically invest $80–$200/month for a comprehensive stack. The key is that your tools should save you more time than they cost. A good baseline is [PostEverywhere Starter at $19/month](https://posteverywhere.ai/pricing) plus CapCut Free.
  
