  ## Hook Strategies That Stop the Scroll
  
  TikTok measures early retention as a primary ranking factor. Strong hooks maintain 80-90% of viewers through the first 3 seconds. Videos starting with immediate value outperform introductions by 30-40% in retention.
  
  According to Smmnut's 2025 research, you have roughly one-third of users scrolling away in under three seconds if your video doesn't instantly grab them.
  
  ### Highest-Performing Hook Categories
  
  **Curiosity-Driven Hooks** (Best performers):
  
  - "You'll never guess what happens next…"
  - "I was today years old when I learned this…"
  - "The secret to \[achieving something\] is simpler than you think…"
  - "Nobody talks about this but…"
  
  **Problem-Solution Hooks**:
  
  - "Struggling with \[common issue\]? Here's how to fix it…"
  - "You've been doing \[something\] wrong. Here's the right way…"
  - "Stop doing \[thing\]. Do this instead…"
  
  **Pattern Interrupt Hooks**:
  
  - "Wait, this doesn't make sense…" (with confusing visual)
  - "Before you scroll, look at this…"
  - Starting mid-action or mid-sentence
  
  ### Retention Techniques That Work
  
  Pattern interrupts every 3-5 seconds keep viewers watching. According to Opus Clip's data, videos with pattern interrupts every 4 seconds average 58% retention versus 41% for static videos.
  
  Essential retention tactics:
  
  - Text overlays appearing at key moments
  - B-roll switches every 3-4 seconds
  - Zoom transitions on important points
  - Captions (12% higher retention with captions)
  - Movement in every frame
  
